WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.750
- So, let's talk about it.

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:02.870
I know people probably
ask you all the time,

00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:04.530
but I love Priyanka and you know this.

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:06.120
- Me too!
- She is so cool,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:10.370
but I didn't realize like how fast, well--

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.480
Okay, what was your first
date like, first of all.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.641
- Well it's kind of a long
story, but I'll tell it.

00:00:15.641 --> 00:00:18.310
- Synopsis.
- So basically, we were told

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.130
by a mutual friend that we should meet.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.810
And he said, "I'll connect you guys".

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.010
He never did, and I got impatient,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.910
so I direct messaged her on Twitter.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.170
- Get it.
- And she responded.

00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:30.010
We talked you know, back and
forth about a year on text,

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:31.450
and then we finally met in person.

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:32.830
It wasn't really a date.

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.320
We just met in person
and went for a drink.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.360
And then about a year later,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.110
we went on our first official
date to the Hollywood Bowl

00:00:39.110 --> 00:00:41.110
to go see the Beauty And The Beast Live.

00:00:42.007 --> 00:00:42.840
- That's adorable!

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.230
- You know, just recently we played there

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.980
to kind of end the first leg of the tour,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.050
and she sat two boxes
away from where we sat

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:49.137
on our first date, it was very cool.

00:00:49.137 --> 00:00:50.890
- That's so cool!

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:52.540
So what I didn't know
though was that y'all got,

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.310
y'all got married pretty quickly.

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.850
I heard people kept going,
"Whoa, that's moving fast."

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.540
First of all, stay in your lane, okay?

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.780
- Exactly, mind your own business.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.070
- So mind yourself.

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:03.637
- No I think, you know,
when you know, you know.

00:01:03.637 --> 00:01:05.660
And we heard that pretty
much from everybody

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:07.870
once we told people we were engaged.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:10.230
But, you know, it's it
was kind of magical.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:13.890
You know, just within eight, nine weeks,

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:15.940
we were talking about marriage.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.419
And within 10, 11 weeks, we were engaged.

00:01:18.419 --> 00:01:19.252
- [Kelly] That's amazing!

00:01:19.252 --> 00:01:21.210
- And we got married
in December last year,

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:23.130
so our one year is coming up on the first.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.250
- That's so exciting.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.070
Congratulations, it's really very cool.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:28.737
To find someone you love like
that to be your best friend,

00:01:28.737 --> 00:01:29.737
it's so cool.

00:01:29.737 --> 00:01:32.610
So, I heard when I was doing the,

00:01:32.610 --> 00:01:33.880
I was reading the pre-interview for this,

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.027
I had no idea that y'all
opened for me in 2005.

00:01:36.027 --> 00:01:39.000
'Cause I feel like I just got really cool.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.660
- No, so, no one cared about us in 2005,

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.470
we were just coming up and
basically, to get other gigs,

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.040
we listed the other acts
that we'd opened up for.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:50.610
But that really just meant that
we were on the outside stage

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.771
in the parking lot while you
were playing for 40,000 people.

00:01:53.771 --> 00:01:54.604
- Still the same.

00:01:54.604 --> 00:01:56.590
- But you helped us get
a lot of gigs after that,

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.440
so thank you.
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.677
- We owe you 20%.

00:01:58.677 --> 00:02:01.260
(everybody laughing)

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.870
- So, now you're on tour for real.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.140
So tell us about Happiness Begins.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:08.660
- Yeah, so this has been
quite the crazy year

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.930
for the family.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:11.950
You know, just a year ago right now,

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:15.173
we had just started recording
music together again.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:19.990
And you know, looking a year
later, we're finishing up

00:02:19.990 --> 00:02:22.310
the first leg of a crazy tour,

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.140
and also the album "Happiness Begins",

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.470
but it all started with a documentary,

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:28.830
which we call "Chasing Happiness",

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:31.370
which was kinda just to tell
our story of our childhood.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.010
You know, our father was a pastor,

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:35.860
we had a pretty crazy
journey in the church,

00:02:35.860 --> 00:02:38.420
and then into our music career together.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.570
We had really no intention

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:41.680
of getting the band back together.

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.470
But after filming for a little while,

00:02:43.470 --> 00:02:46.820
and kind of healing some
of those family wounds

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:48.580
that were there from our
years of working together

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:51.480
in the past, we were able to
look at this with a fresh view

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.200
and really kind of all in different ways,

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.350
find our happiness.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:57.730
And so we went for it, and it's
been an unforgettable year.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:59.470
It's been really amazing.
- That's really cool,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.840
like not only, I mean, I get
like, the fans are excited

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.370
about it, but it's way more
cool for you and your family.

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:06.140
Like, that's a hard thing to like,

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.610
I mean, that's my road family over there,

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:09.580
and it's hard to all be
together all the time,

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.147
especially when you're related.
I can't even imagine that.

00:03:11.147 --> 00:03:12.448
That's really cool that that's ended--

00:03:12.448 --> 00:03:14.070
- It's really special to
share that with family.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.570
- If the documentary,
would you have released it

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.930
if y'all wouldn't have gotten together?

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.910
- I think so, yeah I think, you know,

00:03:18.910 --> 00:03:20.516
we had spent money making it,
so we probably would have.

00:03:20.516 --> 00:03:22.664
(everybody laughing)

00:03:22.664 --> 00:03:25.270
And I think it was an
important story to tell,

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.690
you know, and that was kind of, I think,

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:29.630
the thing that was to us,
so special about it is that

00:03:29.630 --> 00:03:31.060
there was no intention to come back

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:31.940
and do this again from the beginning,

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.260
but when we actually just sat
down and did the hard work

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:35.720
that, you know, most families have to do.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.280
We all go through things
with people we love,

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.290
and whether it's the
family you choose or blood.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.470
- It's usually the ones
you love the most, yeah.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:41.889
- Yeah, you gotta go through it.

00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:44.790
And we did, and we look at the other side

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.420
and we're all kind of in
the best place in our lives.

00:03:47.420 --> 00:03:48.253
- I know you're all
married now, like yeah.

00:03:48.253 --> 00:03:50.770
- All married, my brother's got two kids,

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:53.120
and it's a beautiful time,
and to have been able

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.950
to go through that with your
family is, I think we're all

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:59.594
really grateful and aware of
how unique it is, and so--

00:03:59.594 --> 00:04:02.233
- So cool, I will say, you have like,

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:05.950
the most famous family ever. (laughing)

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:08.840
I was like, looking at everyone
listed in your family tree,

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:11.907
I'm like, "Okay, well, those
kids are gonna be like,

00:04:11.907 --> 00:04:13.720
"they're not gonna know what normal is."

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.170
- They're gonna have some
cool aunts and cool uncles.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.540
- It's amazing, y'all should
have, no you shouldn't,

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:21.040
but you should have a reality
show, I just wanna see it.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.660
I just wanna, I wanna watch the dynamic

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.790
of all those famous people
in one family, that's insane.

00:04:25.790 --> 00:04:27.180
- I think the band might break up again

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:28.013
if we had a reality show.

00:04:28.013 --> 00:04:28.846
(everybody laughing)

00:04:28.846 --> 00:04:30.650
- If cameras were there
all the time, no you won't.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:32.490
You have to be on point.

00:04:32.490 --> 00:04:34.900
Do you have a favorite song on the tour?

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.940
- I have a few that I love.

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.897
It's like picking a favorite
kid, I guess, I can't pick one.

00:04:38.897 --> 00:04:39.880
- Yeah, they're different vibes.

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:41.480
- I'm so connected to my songwriting too,

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:42.930
that it's hard to pick one.

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.930
But we actually have just come out with

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:46.214
a Christmas song,
- I love Christmas.

00:04:46.214 --> 00:04:48.500
- Which has been a dream
of ours forever, me too.

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:49.333
It's my favorite.

00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:50.380
- Wait, y'all don't
have a Christmas album?

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.750
- We have an album--
- What's wrong with you?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.130
- Back in the day with Disney,

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.090
we did a few just songs here and there,

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:57.990
but this is like our
first real swing at doing

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.720
a Christmas song with the
same group of writers,

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.140
producers that we work with
in the rest of our music.

00:05:02.140 --> 00:05:04.720
- Oh my gosh, do a whole
album, I love Christmas music.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:05.910
- As long as you come
on and do it with us.

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.550
- I will sing with you!

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.265
- You already sang with John--
- Unless you're just joking.

00:05:09.265 --> 00:05:10.098
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:05:10.098 --> 00:05:11.970
I did sing with John.

00:05:11.970 --> 00:05:14.440
I love Christmas music.
- Me too.

00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.010
- I think it's so cool 'cause
you can get away with like

00:05:16.010 --> 00:05:17.120
that cheesy good feeling.
- When do you start playing

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.960
Christmas music?
- I actually started,

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:22.120
and my staff will tell you,
I actually started like

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:24.260
two months ago, 'cause I was
wrapping presents in Montana,

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:25.340
we have a ranch there, and I was

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.660
wrapping Christmas presents.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.230
- So two months ago, so like September?

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:29.063
- Yeah.
- Wow.

00:05:29.063 --> 00:05:30.451
- Never too early!

00:05:30.451 --> 00:05:31.600
(everybody laughing)

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.250
Because I was wrapping Christmas presents!

00:05:33.250 --> 00:05:34.920
November, December are really busy,

00:05:34.920 --> 00:05:36.637
so I was having to do
everything before hand, and so--

00:05:36.637 --> 00:05:37.953
- You did say that you were
wrapping Christmas presents--

00:05:37.953 --> 00:05:40.130
- I was wrapping Christmas presents, yes.

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.400
- That's impressive.
- I do that.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:43.090
- I start shopping three days before.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:43.923
(audience laughing)

00:05:43.923 --> 00:05:45.776
- Yeah, so does my husband,
which is why I do it.

00:05:45.776 --> 00:05:49.093
- Yeah, yeah.
(Kelly laughs)

